# mutgap_disp_iosfc_v1_planes_upgraded: A v1 descriptor's seven planes are each copied into the v2 form the map works on. The device first maps a v2 descriptor whose planes 1-6 have five components (NoMemory), leaving those bytes in the heap block the next map's descriptor may reuse; then, switched to v1, it maps seven good 16 x 8 planes of 1 x 1 elements, each based at its offset and with four 8-bit components (success; a plane left unconverted would carry other bytes), one such plane (success), and one plane whose components' bit offsets are 1, 3, 5 and 200, which IOSurface accepts too: the offsets are only metadata.
{"iosfc": true, "op": "config", "ram": [["0x40000000", "0x4000000"]], "stamp_slots": 2, "watchdog_s": 30}
